    }
   ],
   "gap": "The construction or argument and the full treatment promised by proved=annex:p15.product-bernoulli-boundaries are missing for two conclusions promised at body lines 262-265. The annex (lines 397-400) cites only 'the affinity summability criterion' (thm:p15-product-affinity-series), which yields mu<<nu iff sum eps_m^2<infinity. (i) The reverse direction nu<<mu is neither argued nor cited, yet 'The laws are equivalent exactly when sum eps_m^2<infinity' and 'eps_m=1/(4m) gives equivalence' both need it: the proof never states that Bernoulli coordinates with p_m,q_m in (0,1) are equivalent and never appeals to the reverse-measure part of thm:p15-product-affinity-criterion. (ii) The claimed singularity for eps_m=1/(4 sqrt m) rests on the words 'giving the two examples', with no written step sum(1-h_m)=infinity => H_infinity=0 => mu perp nu. The failure condition 'missing promised direction/case' therefore holds.",
